Build 1.2.8 - 2026-08-16 - SIX BUGS FROM THE OWNER'S PHONE, AND WHAT THEY UNCOVERED

The owner listed six faults from the live app and asked for them one at a time,
fixed after the listing was finished. All six are done. Three of them turned out
to be worse than reported, and every one of them had shipped because the screen
it was on had never been photographed.

  typecheck 0 · 1,861 tests pass · production build 0
  112 screenshots · ZERO layout problems · zero non-fixture errors

VERSION IS 1.2.8. Build #95 carried 1.2.7 and this is different code.

WHAT HE REPORTED, AND WHAT IT ACTUALLY WAS

 1. LOG OUT NOT REACHABLE. Members were right and it was not vague. Measured,
    the bottom of the Logout button against the bottom of the screen:

        360x592   145px BELOW the screen      360x740    19px below
        360x640   104px below                 360x800+   fine

    On any phone under about 780px of usable height a member COULD NOT LOG OUT.
    The sheet capped itself at 85% of the screen, stacked three blocks inside,
    and nothing scrolled — so the footer was what got pushed off. Structural,
    not a number: the grid gives way now and the footer is pinned.

    His follow-up — "all buttons are not showing some hiding" — was also right.
    The first fix bought a reachable Logout with hidden actions. Tiles were
    tightened instead: nothing hidden at 640 and above, no scrolling at all.
    Labels went UP from 9px to 10px and out of all-caps.

 2. CREATE POST, "many times not working". He answered that nothing opens at
    all, and that is one `catch`. Android's picker rejects both when a member
    backs out AND when it cannot open; the code returned "nobody chose
    anything" for both, and the composer closes on that. A picker that failed
    to open was a button that did nothing and said nothing. Only a message
    containing "cancel" counts as cancelling now; anything else says so and
    falls back to the OS file browser, which does not use that plugin at all.

 3+4. THE CROP DIALOG. "any of options not wokring" was EIGHTEEN TAP TARGETS
    UNDER 44px — close button 16x16, every zoom/rotate/mirror button 20x20,
    aspect chips 35x27. Drawn for a mouse, shipped to a thumb.

    And underneath it, the one that matters most in this build:

    ZOOM SILENTLY CROPPED THE WRONG PART OF THE PHOTOGRAPH.

        zoom 100%   element 270x480   picture 270x480   scale used 3.33  true 3.33
        zoom 200%   element 540x480   picture 270x480   scale used 1.67  true 3.33

    Anyone who zoomed got a crop from somewhere else in the frame, off by the
    zoom factor plus a 135px offset — and at high zoom the read area leaves the
    image entirely and nothing is drawn, which is the blank "After" panel he
    photographed. One cause, two reports. Verified correct at 100/200/400% on
    portrait, landscape and square after the fix.

    Also: body scroll lock, the back gesture closes the dialog instead of
    unwinding the route beneath it, pinch-to-zoom, thirds guide, and corner
    handles split into a 14px viewfinder bracket over a 44px invisible target —
    he asked for smaller marks, and smaller alone would have made them
    impossible to grab, which was his other complaint about the same screen.

 5+6. THE WALL'S ABOUT PANEL AND THE ACCOUNT PAGE. Measured off his screenshot:
    370px of screen to show an email address and a join date. Thirteen outlined
    cards on one, nine boxes on the other, a 36px grey disc behind every 16px
    glyph, a caption under each value repeating what the icon already said, and
    the bio printed TWICE on the same screen. One 44px row per fact now, no
    outlines anywhere — his standing rule, stated four times in three days.

THE PATTERN UNDER ALL SIX

Every one of these was on a screen the sweep had never rendered. The crop
dialog is mounted from nine places and had no scene. The account sheet is an
overlay, so no page scene drew it. The About tab opens from a menu into
component state, so 100% of this project's screenshots of that page were the
photo grid. Four new scenes close those, and `?section=about|works` makes About
linkable as a side effect.

THE CHECKER ITSELF WAS WRONG THREE TIMES, and each was found by using it:
  · it called a modal's own backdrop a navigation bar and reported 74 items
    "hidden" — it compared rectangles and could not see z-order;
  · it read a button mid-animation as 35x35 when the layout says 44 (measured
    at 0.9 scale and 1.6% opacity — it was barely on screen);
  · it never rendered the build label beside Logout, because the Capacitor stub
    had no App plugin — so the footer row it had been photographing was not the
    row members see, with Logout at full width instead of half.
All three fixed, and each broken deliberately afterwards to prove the alarm
still fires.

WHAT ONLY THE PHONE CAN ANSWER

  1. Open the account sheet on a short phone. Every action visible, Logout at
     the bottom, V1095-style build label to its left.
  2. Post a photo, then CROP AND ZOOM IN before uploading. The saved crop must
     be the part you framed. This is the fix that matters most.
  3. Pinch the photo in the crop dialog. Press the back gesture — it should
     close the dialog, not the page.
  4. If Create Post fails again, you should now get a MESSAGE saying why, and
     the file browser should open. Send me that message.
  5. Your wall's About panel, and the Profile page: no boxes, no repeated bio.

NOT DONE, AND NOT CLAIMED

